---
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { contact, legal } from '../config';
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms of use"
  kicker="Terms"
  description="The short terms for using playrunqa.com: what you may reuse, what the information here is, and which law applies."
  lead="Short, because there is not much to say. These terms cover this website, a personal portfolio, and nothing else."
>
  <section class="row">
    <h2>Who this site belongs to</h2>
    <p>
      playrunqa.com is run by {legal.controller}{legal.address ? `, ${legal.address}` : `, ${contact.location}`}. Questions
      go to <a href={`mailto:${contact.email}`}>{contact.email}</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2>The name, the logo and the content</h2>
    <p>
      The PlayRun name, the logo and the icon, the pixel artwork, the words and the code of this site are mine. They
      are not licensed for reuse. You may link to any page. The typefaces and the game logos belong to other people
      and are credited below.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2>The information here</h2>
    <p>
      Everything on this site is given in good faith and kept as accurate as I can make it, but it comes with no
      guarantee. It describes my experience and is not an offer of any kind.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>
      Some links lead to other sites, for example store pages on Steam, LinkedIn or the ICO. I do not control
      them and I am not responsible for what they show or how they treat your data.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2>The games on the site</h2>
    <p>
      The runner, the bug hunt and the achievements are optional play. They can be switched off with the HUD button and
      they are off under a reduced motion setting. The site works fully without them.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="row">
    <h2>Which law applies</h2>
    <p>These terms are governed by the law of England and Wales, and the courts of England and Wales have jurisdiction.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="row" id="credits">
    <h2>Credits and trademarks</h2>
    <p>Typefaces: Pixel Operator by Jayvee Enaguas (CC0); Montserrat by Julieta Ulanovsky and contributors (SIL Open Font License).</p>
    <p>Game names and logos are trademarks of their respective owners, shown only to identify games I have worked on. No endorsement is implied.</p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
